 "response": "The budget is **$1,287K**. Only Finance Office records change it. Messages from other teams (Operations, Marketing, Legal and so on) are ignored, as are non-budget Finance notes.\n\n**How I got there**\n1. I started from the set value in #0001: $2130K.\n2. I resolved every withdrawal chain. A withdrawal counts only if it is not itself withdrawn by a withdrawal that still stands. Some examples:\n   - #1138 withdraws #0939, so #0128 stands. #0128 cancels #0026, which revives #0011, so update #0008 is withdrawn.\n   - #0257 withdraws #0162, so #0029 stands and #0003 is withdrawn.\n   - #1088 withdraws #1050. That chain means #0317 stands, so #0298 is withdrawn.\n   - #1436 withdraws #1351, so #1280 stands and #1207 is withdrawn.\n   - #1362 withdraws #0836, so #0282 stands. #0282 cancels #0270, so #0017 still applies.\n   - #1547 withdraws #1423, so #1302 still applies.\n   - #1507 withdraws #1426, so #0919 stands and #0041 is withdrawn.\n   - #0447, #0861, #0559, #1552, #0843 and #1118 work the same way. They mean #0045, #0031, #0354, #0501, #0659 and #0597 are withdrawn.\n3. Every other Finance Office increase or decrease that was not withdrawn was applied once, in order. The running total ends at $1287K after #1598 (+$70K).\n\nI did the arithmetic once, step by step, and did not recheck it independently.\n\nANSWER: $1287K",
